          "completionSummary": "P-007 DONE — SideStage apps/api serves the shared reconnect-safe scout streaming contract, verified LIVE against :3100. (This call re-sends the same close with verifiedHow + test results attached to settle completion authority; no scope change.)\n\nSHIPPED (apps/api/src/scout/ unless noted): scout.types.ts (wire union ScoutStreamEvent + ScoutStreamRequest resume cursor + ScoutSessionStore seam, pinned to libs/scout-chat reducer's DISPLAY_CHAT_EVENT_TYPES); scout-turn-bus.service.ts NEW (port of Restart's turn-bus — a turn runs DETACHED into a per-turn getChannel() ring buffer, which IS the reconnect property); scout-session.store.ts NEW (transcript seam + pure transcriptVersion/transcriptEtag/visibleTranscript/ifNoneMatchMatches + in-memory fallback); db/pg-scout-session-store.ts NEW (single-statement `messages || EXCLUDED.messages` append so racing turns cannot silently lose one); scout.service.ts (stream() emitting session→tool_start→products→token*→done, plus an OPTIONAL stream?() on ScoutReplyModel so an LLM relays real tokens while the deterministic model gets chunkReply() — indistinguishable on the wire; chat() and stream() share one turn path so they cannot drift); scout.controller.ts (POST /scout/chat/stream via sseResponse+bridgeChannel+sseResponseToNode with X-Scout-Turn-Id and Last-Event-ID replay; GET /scout/session/:id ETag'd — deliberately NOT Nest's @Sse(), which is GET-only and owns the response so it can carry neither a body nor replay); scout.module.ts (PG-or-memory store seam like every other SideStage store); db/schema.sql + db/schema-guard.ts (scout_session in REQUIRED_TABLES so its absence fails boot loudly instead of 500ing per request); apps/api/package.json (+@papercusp/sse, already workspace-linked).\n\nDECISION D-007 recorded: apps/api stays free of @types/express — controllers declare minimal structural req/res shapes (matches @papercusp/sse's deps-free Node bridge; avoids an install in the shared tree, which re-hoisted a package and 500'd the live dev server earlier today). Governs P-012, which extends this same controller.\n\nALSO: restarted the SideStage :3100 API — it was DOWN when I went to verify (nothing listening; unsupervised). Logging to /tmp/sidestage-logs/api-3100.log.",
