      "contentHash": "504815ef114af0ae108875faa84da51c03c99cecb3b6d6ac4cd40d3eca207489",
      "markdown": "---\ntitle: SideStage Active Event tabbed Inventory utility rail\nslug: sidestage-active-event-tabbed-inventory-rail-2026-08-14\nstatus: ready\ncreated: 2026-08-15\nupdated: 2026-08-15\n---\n\n# SideStage Active Event tabbed Inventory utility rail\n\n## Now\n\n**State:** Draft. Plan body to be filled in.\n\n**Next:** human reviews scope and lists Phase 1 items.\n\n## Background\n\n(Why this plan exists; what problem it addresses.)\n\n## Phase 1 — TODO\n\n(Use plans:add-item to populate. Each item is one line:\nsingle id, status token, free text, optional blocked-by.)\n\n\n## Phase — Implementation\n\n- **P-001** `done` Implement the production Tabbed utility rail: add a compact Active Event inventory panel using the existing event.actions.items, event.adjustStock, and event.addItems seams; register it beside Run of Show in the dock; migrate saved layouts idempotently; add the mobile Inventory mode; ship focused unit and regression tests. importance: high — note: ← WI-39210 completed (done)\n- **P-002** `done` Run focused SideStage web tests and typecheck, repair every failure, and record exact verification evidence. blocked-by: P-001 importance: high — note: ← WI-39215 completed (done)\n- **P-003** `todo` Verify the Active Event Inventory tab end to end on desktop and mobile with Verdict, including tab switching, quantity controls, add-item affordance, responsive layout, console, and network health; then close the plan. blocked-by: P-002 importance: high\n\n\n\n## Decisions\n\n(Use plans:add-decision to append. Each decision is a third-level\nheading with a date line and a body paragraph.)\n\n### D-001 — Implement the owner-selected Tabbed utility rail by extending existing event and dock seams\nDate: 2026-08-15\nDate: 2026-08-15\nAvi selected the Tabbed utility rail and authorized self-directed implementation. Inventory becomes a peer dock tab beside Run of Show on Active Event, while the existing standalone Inventory route remains available for full-catalog editing. The utility panel reuses event.actions.items, event.adjustStock, event.addItems, EventCreationPanel, and dock-workbench persistence; no parallel inventory API or store is introduced. Existing saved Active Event layouts are migrated in place so geometry is preserved, and Run of Show remains the initially selected tab to avoid disrupting live-show continuity. Low stock is defined as three or fewer event-reserved units and surfaced in the Inventory tab title.\nRelated: P-001, P-002, P-003\n\n### D-002 — Studio inventory is store-scoped, not Demo User-scoped\nDate: 2026-08-15\nAvi corrected the product contract on 2026-08-15: Studio inventory reads and writes bind to the stable Studio/store seller principal. For the current single-store demo, that principal is the legacy demo-seller. Switching the global Demo User may change buyer, Watch, Orders, chat, or other identity-sensitive behavior, but must never change Studio inventory. Do not restore or extend the prior auto-generated-principal folding behavior; future multi-store support requires an explicit store/workspace selector and authorization seam.\nRelated: P-001\n",
