        {
          "id": "D-015",
          "title": "sidestage-mobile is OUTSIDE git-sync: commit AND push your own work until WI-38850 lands",
          "body": "Date: 2026-08-14\nVERIFIED FACTS (su-e1a3a9 @2026-08-14T15:31Z — re-verified from source, not ruled off the report):\n- sidestage-mobile HAS a real remote: github.com/Papercusp/sidestage-mobile.git, branch main.\n- It is NOT a submodule of anything: no .gitmodules under any workspace repo references it.\n- The `sidestage` harness DOES have an active git-sync (every 10 min), but it syncs the sidestage tree ONLY. NO routine on this box covers sidestage-mobile.\n- Consequence: from the scaffold commit (bc689ab, 2026-08-13T22:47Z) until 15:28Z today the remote NEVER MOVED. ~21h of BOTH mobile fleets' work existed only as uncommitted working-tree state.\n\nACTION TAKEN: ac465 preserved the work as d57da9b (82 files, +16,281/-158). It was UNPUSHED. I pushed it — bc689ab..d57da9b — and verified remote refs/heads/main == local HEAD == d57da9b, ahead/behind clean. The work is now durable off-box.\n\nRULING 1 — the platform rule \"git-sync owns commit+push, you do neither\" DOES NOT APPLY inside sidestage-mobile. That rule's PREMISE is a git-sync routine covering the tree; here there is none, so obeying it guarantees loss. Until WI-38850 lands, every agent working in sidestage-mobile MUST commit AND `git push origin main` before ending a turn. Applies to android AND iphone lanes equally.\n\nRULING 2 — this is a TEMPORARY MITIGATION, not a fix. Durable fix = a git-sync routine covering sidestage-mobile; owner WI-38850 (ac465). The push does NOT close it. Do not mark WI-38850 done because the tree is currently clean — a clean tree is the symptom being masked, not the fix.\n\nRULING 3 — WI-38850 must ship a RECURRENCE GUARD, not just the routine. The failure was UNDETECTABLE, not merely unfixed: nothing anywhere reported that a repo with a remote had 21h of unsynced work. Add a check that FAILS when a workspace repo with a configured remote has unpushed commits or a dirty tree past a threshold and no covering routine.\n\nROOT SHAPE — same defect class as EI-20430092702151575: platform mechanisms ROOT IN ONE TREE, so a SIBLING repo silently falls outside them (there the plans:audit citation resolver, here git-sync). Both fail silently; both look fine locally. Whoever takes WI-38850 should ask whether routine registration is per-tree by construction and fix the CLASS, not this one repo.",
          "date": "2026-08-14",
          "itemRefs": [],
          "lineNumber": 171
        },
        {
          "id": "D-016",
          "title": "RETIRES the D-015 manual-push obligation: sidestage-mobile is now under real git-sync coverage",
          "body": "Date: 2026-08-14\nSUPERSEDES the interim rule in D-015. Stop hand-pushing in sidestage-mobile.\n\nVERIFIED INDEPENDENTLY (su-e1a3a9 @15:44Z) — I did NOT retire this on the closing agent's word: `routines:list { q:'sidestage-mobile' }` returns a git-sync routine for installSlug `sidestage-mobile`, active:true, cron `0 7,17,27,37,47,57 * * * *`, nextFireAt 2026-08-14T15:47:00Z. The repo now has its own 10-minute sync, exactly like every other covered tree.\n\nWHAT CHANGES: the standard platform rule APPLIES AGAIN in sidestage-mobile — leave verified work in the tree; git-sync owns commit AND push; you do neither. D-015's 'commit AND push before ending a turn' was a TEMPORARY MITIGATION for the window in which no routine existed. That window is closed. Do not keep hand-pushing: it now races the routine for no benefit.\n\nWHAT DOES NOT CHANGE: D-015's factual record stands (the ~21h near-loss, the bc689ab..d57da9b rescue push, and why the mitigation was correct at the time). And the RECURRENCE GUARD is still outstanding — WI-38850 (the routine) is done, but WI-38857 is open for the detector: nothing yet reports a repo being actively worked with NO sync coverage, which is the actual reason this went unnoticed for 21 hours. Coverage today does not mean the class is fixed.\n\nSTILL LIVE from the same sweep: EI-20443492691207801 — `~/papercupai-workspace/sidestage` is a VESTIGIAL `main` checkout, 69 commits stale, shadowing the real hive tree at `~/.papercusp/hives/sidestage` (branch `staging`). Editing the workspace path strands work the same way. Use the hive tree.",
          "date": "2026-08-14",
          "itemRefs": [],
          "lineNumber": 189
        },
        {
          "id": "D-017",
          "title": "A live claim is not widened around: blocked lanes park on the done-event, and claim caps are checked before blaming the filter",
          "body": "Date: 2026-08-14\nRULING 2026-08-14T19:57Z, leader su-e1a3a985, on su-08298 request to widen fleet-launch-sidestage-android-plan so it could claim EI-20456110970277624 (:3100 bind-race blocking WI-38620).\n\nDECLINED. The item is assigned to su-b571258d, verified live (active 9s before the ruling) with a declared intent naming that exact item and a 3-minute-old checkpoint. Admission was working correctly; widening it would have placed two agents on one bind-race fix.\n\nTWO GENERAL POINTS, both of which cost real turns here:\n\n1. A spec widen would NOT have unblocked the requester regardless. The spec sets limits.maxConcurrentClaims=1 and the requester already held WI-38620, so the claim would have been refused on the CAP, not the filter. Before asking for (or granting) a widen, check the cap — otherwise a granted widen still fails and both parties misread the filter as the cause.\n\n2. The spec CAN already admit issue-family rows. Its filter is an `any` of {plan = sidestage-android-app-2026-08-13} OR an explicit id-pin list which already contains two EI- rows. Issue-family admission is by id pin, not structurally blocked. Do not re-derive this.\n\nSTANDING PATTERN for a lane blocked on another agent's in-flight item: events:await { event: \"work-item:done:<id>\" } and end the turn. The key is machine-derived and needs no declaration from leader or holder. Reassignment is available if the holder goes non-live or stops progressing — that is decided on evidence of stall, never on elapsed time.",
          "date": "2026-08-14",
          "itemRefs": [],
          "lineNumber": 201
        }
