          "id": "D-008",
          "title": "D-008 — Ledger reconcile of all 12 gap items against D-006/D-007, ruled at ACCEPTANCE-CLAUSE level (not at build-green level)",
          "body": "Date: 2026-08-17\nBy su-aa261e73 under WI-39711, on leader su-6613215b's ASAP reconcile directive (msxh1nsm). Input: D-006 + D-007 (clean-clone re-baseline by su-7c55c214 at 4bfc31f, green twice). The clone was NOT re-run; D-007 is taken as measured fact.\n\nMETHOD: D-007 graded by what the green clean-clone PROVED. This re-grades each item against its own written Acceptance clause. A green build satisfies a clause only where the clause is about the build. Three verdicts diverge from the directive's grouping under that test; each is evidenced below. D-007's three method caveats (non-default ports 3399/5399, no docker compose so 13 PG tests self-skip, green build != product correctness) are discharged by NO close here.\n\n== DONE ==\nP-002 — SATISFIED, directly measured. Acceptance is literally \"all three commands exit zero twice from a clean worktree\"; D-007 measured exactly that (install/typecheck/test/build exit 0; 1,736 pass / 13 skip / 0 fail; twice). Sub-clause \"top-level test command reaches the web suite\" CONFIRMED this turn: test => test:deploy && test:libs && test:apps, and test:apps runs `npm run test --workspace @papercusp/sidestage-web`. Mirror WI-39258 closes with it.\n\nP-007 — SATISFIED by landed tests; every acceptance-bearing clause has an exact test:\n- \"duplicates apply once\" -> action.service.test.ts:187 'returns one audited result for concurrent retries with the same client request id'\n- \"rollback refuses to erase a newer seller action\" -> action.service.test.ts:340 'rejects rollback after a newer write changes the same item' (impl intent: action-item.store.ts:27)\n- restart-safe idempotency / recovery-readback -> action.service.test.ts:310 'replays and rolls back a client request after the service restarts on the same stores'\n- optimistic rollback / concurrency -> action-item.store.test.ts:68 'rejects stale optimistic writes without partially mutating the lineup'\n\n== DROPPED (superseded, NOT achieved) ==\nP-001 — its executable half is OBE: it exists to capture clean-checkout FAILURES as fixtures, and D-007 proves none remain, so it cannot be run as written. Its surviving deliverable — the requirement matrix separating clean-clone evidence from the moving shared tree — is NOT done and is ALSO required verbatim by P-012 (\"the full assignment matrix with Verdict\"). Dropped as superseded rather than done, so the ledger never asserts a matrix that does not exist; residue carried by P-012.\n\n== STAYS OPEN, narrowed ==\nP-006 — NOT closed. Half satisfied, and the unmet half is contradicted by a LANDED TEST, not merely unproven. Acceptance: \"rejected decisions are durable evidence but never mutate business state\". The POLICY path does write rejected audits (policy.service.ts:472 action:'rejected' -> policy_audit_entry). The GUARDED-ACTION path deliberately writes NONE: action.service.test.ts:299 'blocks below-floor writes before mutating state or creating an audit' asserts listAudit(...) toEqual([]). \"Never mutate business state\" holds (price stays 1_500). So the rejected-action-audit clause is landed as its OPPOSITE. Residue: decide whether P-006 wants durable rejected GUARDED-ACTION audits (then this is a real gap AND a test encoding the wrong contract) or only policy-side rejections (then P-006 is closeable after re-scoping). Also unruled: \"no duplicate audit system\" — policy_audit_entry and action_audit_entry coexist; plausibly two domains, not assessed.\n\nP-012 — NOT closed, against the directive's grouping. It is the clean-clone SUBMISSION gate and only its build legs ran. Executed by D-007: setup, dev smoke, test, typecheck, build. NOT executed by anyone: restart/durability checks, real-provider benchmark, the assignment matrix with Verdict, \"ship normally and repeat critical production flows\", and its acceptance proper — production clean, critical APIs 2xx, tested/deployed commit matches, reviewer packet with commands, results, latency, safety cases, screenshots, rollback instructions. No reviewer packet exists. Closing it would report a PASSED submission gate during a submission push — the most costly possible false close. This also resolves an internal inconsistency in the directive, which asked to close P-012 while unfreezing its own mirror WI-39268. If another lane holds evidence for the unrun legs, the leader may close it citing that; this declines to assert it unproven.\n\nP-010 — still real per D-007 (README Quick start never tells a reviewer to seed; following it verbatim very likely yields a running app with NO demo event). 7c55c did not run the docker path: strong indication, not a reproduction. Claimable.\n\nP-003, P-004, P-005, P-008, P-009, P-011 — NOT ASSESSED by anyone; behavioural/product items a green build says nothing about. D-007 explicitly says not to read it as clearing them. Claimable, unassessed; assessment is the leader's live walkthrough, not this lane.\n\nNET: 2 done (P-002, P-007), 1 dropped (P-001), 9 claimable (P-003/4/5/6/8/9/10/11/12). Not-firmly-resolved residue is NINE, not three.\nRelated: P-001, P-002, P-003, P-004, P-005, P-006, P-007, P-008, P-009, P-010, P-011, P-012",
