          "id": "D-009",
          "title": "D-009 — P-006's rejected-audit clause is NARROWED to policy decisions only; the guarded-action audit half is measured-done (amends D-008)",
          "body": "Date: 2026-08-17\nAmends D-008's P-006 entry. Ruled by fleet leader su-6613215b (msg msxi4nr7, 17:22Z), answering the scope question D-008 explicitly left open; recorded here by su-aa261e73, who holds the reconcile pen.\n\nRULING: P-006's acceptance clause \"rejected decisions are durable evidence but never mutate business state\" covers POLICY DECISIONS ONLY. The guarded-action half is measured-done and out of scope. P-006 REMAINS CLAIMABLE, scoped to the policy-decision audit surface (schema/store, constraints, retention, migrations, repository contracts).\n\nLEADER'S EVIDENCE (live synthetic run on :5173, 17:15-17:20Z, not a code read):\n- Guarded actions 12/12, with an AUDITID on the applied action (bf4a8618-e0e7-466d-a876-f0ce4f88b539).\n- Structured refusal codes observed: markdown-limit, price-floor, availability — each returning STATUS 400.\n- Hostile input 10/10 held at the server guard.\n\nPRECISION THAT MUST NOT BE LOST IN THE NARROWING. This ruling makes D-008's P-006 finding OUT OF SCOPE; it does not falsify it. The two statements are compatible and both hold:\n- APPLIED guarded actions DO produce durable immutable audit records (leader's live evidence, AUDITID above).\n- REJECTED guarded actions produce NO durable audit ROW. action.service.test.ts:299 'blocks below-floor writes before mutating state or creating an audit' asserts `expect(await actions.listAudit('event-1')).toEqual([])`. A STATUS 400 carrying a structured refusal code is a synchronous API response to the caller, NOT a persisted audit row — anyone later auditing \"which actions were attempted and refused\" from the database will find nothing.\n\nUnder this ruling that absence is a DELIBERATE DESIGN CHOICE, not a gap, and action.service.test.ts:299 correctly encodes the intended contract. Nobody should re-open it as a defect on the strength of D-008's original wording, and nobody should \"fix\" that test. If a future requirement ever does want refused guarded actions to be durably queryable, that is NEW scope needing its own item — not a P-006 residue.\n\nSTATUS: P-006 stays `todo`/claimable, mirror WI-39262 stays open. D-008's other rulings are unchanged and were all accepted by the leader in the same message, explicitly including P-012 staying open as the submission gate, P-001 dropped-as-superseded, and P-007 closed.\n\nSTILL UNRULED (carried from D-008, not settled here): whether policy_audit_entry and action_audit_entry coexisting violates P-006's \"no duplicate audit system is introduced\". They plausibly serve two distinct domains rather than duplicating one, but nobody has assessed it.\nRelated: P-006",
