          "id": "D-011",
          "title": "sidestage-dev.service is the canonical single dev stack; the terminal npm start:dev stack retires",
          "body": "Date: 2026-08-17\nCONTEXT: Two sidestage dev stacks run on this box, BOTH from the same checkout (~/.papercusp/hives/sidestage, staging): (A) systemd user unit sidestage-dev.service — enabled, durable, declares \"SideStage local API (:3100) and Vite web (:5173)\", up since Aug 16; (B) a GNOME-Terminal `npm run start:dev` (vte-spawn scope, since ~04:30 EDT Aug 17) serving web :5174 and, at the moment, the live api :3100. Every git-sync sweep restarts both stacks' tsx-watch api children, which RACE for :3100; the loser cannot bind and burns PG connections until the next sweep — the mechanism behind dev PG hitting max_connections (EI-20739798038041966; aa261's orphan-kill on Aug 17 dropped sockets 184→106 but is mitigation-only).\n\nRULING: (1) Canonical dev stack = sidestage-dev.service. (2) The terminal stack retires: SIGTERM the npm process tree inside its vte-spawn scope ONLY — never the terminal emulator window — after the owner confirms the window is not load-bearing (asked in the owner's interactive turn, Aug 17 ~22:4xZ). (3) Post-kill verification: the systemd unit's api binds :3100, web stays on :5173, and PG connection count stays flat across two consecutive git-sync sweeps. (4) Interim, until the owner answers: no stack is touched; if connection pressure recurs, re-apply aa261's verified orphan-kill recipe (kill-by-PID with cmdline+cgroup+listen re-verification immediately before signalling). Execution owner: aa261.",
          "date": "2026-08-17",
