          "completionSummary": "P-008 acceptance met and live-proven: \"a missing catalog property triggers labelled fallback through public UI/API and no late/unverified finding can send.\" The feature was BUILT BUT DEAD IN PRODUCTION — the pipeline half existed, every edge was missing. All five edges are landed, and the behaviour is now demonstrated on the running stack with a three-way discriminating probe, not asserted from unit tests.\n\nUI EVIDENCE (isolated Chromium, per the fleet leader's evidence rule msxq5egm — the shared verdict daemon is banned): screenshot /tmp/wi39264-readback-1787001450981.png, driver script /tmp/wi39264-submit-readback.mjs, run 21:17:39Z. Landed URL logged before and after the interaction (http://localhost:5173/?tab=seller&studio=active-event); the wire POST to /copilot/events/test/turns carried [\"capacity-litres\",\"boil-time\"] (I typed 'capacity-litres, , boil-time' and the blank was correctly dropped); server readback of GET /copilot/events/test/proposals showed proposal f202de5f carrying that exact array.\n\nAPI PROOF (event `test`, product Harbor Kettle — catalog attributes are sku/brand/color/condition/productType, NO capacity property):\n  A CONTROL  \"What is the price of the Harbor Kettle?\", no requiredProperties -> status=pending (grounded), 3 citations, context.webFindings=null. Proposal 6ac67836.\n  B TEST     same question + requiredProperties:[\"capacity-litres\"] -> status=blocked, 0 citations, \"I don't have enough verified event or catalog information to answer that yet.\", webFindings=[]. Proposal 63755442.\n  C CONTROL2 same question + requiredProperties:[\"color\"] (present in catalog) -> status=pending, 4 citations including the NEW catalog-product:event-demo-01-v1, and the reply gained an Ember variant the control never mentioned. Proposal f57d7340.\n\nWhy the three together are conclusive: A-vs-B rules out the block being a background artifact (identical question grounds green with the property dropped); B-vs-C rules out \"any requiredProperties value blocks\" (an ANSWERABLE property still grounds, so the gate is about verifiability, not about the field being set). context.webFindings null-vs-[] is the fallback-RAN discriminator — null means the research fallback never ran, [] means it ran and returned no verified web finding. That single field separates \"path is dead\" (the defect this item existed to fix) from \"path ran and correctly refused\". \"Labelled\" is visible in context.sources as {id, kind, label}: the merged fallback finding appears as catalog-product:event-demo-01-v1 / \"Harbor Kettle verified catalog record\".\n\nWHY THIS ALMOST SHIPPED AS A FALSE PASS: my first live attempt returned status:'blocked' and looked like a clean pass. The same question WITHOUT requiredProperties also returned blocked — carrying a Postgres \"sorry, too many clients already\" error inside an HTTP 201 + status:'blocked' envelope, shape-identical to a real policy refusal. The block was an infra artifact. I cleared the DB pressure first (an orphaned API instance holding ~50 connections, killed with the fleet leader's authorisation; sockets to :55434 dropped 184->106) and only then re-ran the probe with controls. Filed EI-20739223188523567 for the underlying product defect: the endpoint conflates an infrastructure failure with a policy block.",
