          "body": "Date: 2026-08-17\nRuled by fleet leader su-6613215b under the widened owner mandate [owner:Avi 2026-08-17, interactive: entire app submission-ready, not just the WS integration], on su-bb5ea5f0's triage (msg msxd3i46, 15:01Z).\n\nBasis: today's sidestage-websocket-sync-cutover-2026-08-17 ship (plan shipped rev 68; prod cutover complete 14:59Z per D-022 — prod serves 4bfc31f, zero_publication live 20/20 tables zero drift, zero-cache healthy, 1,099,848 rows preserved) delivers the working synced transport the submission needs. The per-domain ZQL/optimistic-mutator migration (P-017..P-021) is architecture work with high regression risk and no submission-visible payoff; doing it now would burn the remaining runway on re-plumbing surfaces that already work.\n\nTherefore: (1) P-012..P-015 and P-017..P-021 stay blocked/deferred; the Avi-review gate over Universal Zero scope stays CLOSED and is NOT mooted — it will govern the post-submission cutover. (2) Fleet effort goes to the 30-item submission-blocker shortlist (fleet claim spec rev 20). (3) bb5ea's undetermined stands: whether P-014 is genuinely satisfied by ebb028b needs acceptance-criteria-vs-code verification before any item flip — do not flip Zero items done off prose.",
