      "markdown": "---\ntitle: Enforce SideStage cart principal ownership\nslug: sidestage-cart-principal-boundary-2026-08-15\nstatus: shipped\ncreated: 2026-08-15\nupdated: 2026-08-15\n---\n\n# Enforce SideStage cart principal ownership\n\n## Now\n\n**State:** ⛔ PLAN CLOSED — SHIPPED 2026-08-15. Nothing in this plan is actionable. Anything below this line is the last pre-shipped snapshot, kept for history: it described work that is finished or abandoned, so do not start from it. Read frontmatter `status`, not this prose, to learn whether a plan is live (stamped by plans:set-plan-status).\n\nComplete. Cart aggregates are buyer-bound, every buyer-facing service/controller/sync/web path enforces the canonical principal, and authorization precedes expiration cleanup side effects.\n\n**Next:** none — the plan is shipped. (Pre-shipped next, no longer actionable: No plan work remains; allow the normal commit/checkpoint/deploy pipeline to carry the verified change.)\n\n## Background\n\n(Why this plan exists; what problem it addresses.)\n\n## Phase 1 — TODO\n\n(Use plans:add-item to populate. Each item is one line:\nsingle id, status token, free text, optional blocked-by.)\n\n\n## Phase — Implementation\n\n- **P-001** `done` Bind each newly created cart aggregate to the normalized buyer principal and add service-level owned read/write methods; preserve internal cart lifecycle APIs for trusted server workflows. importance: urgent — note: ← WI-39221 completed (done)\n- **P-002** `done` Require the canonical demo-principal boundary on CartController and cart.byId, route REST fallback requests with the selected buyer principal, and classify the routes as principal-partitioned. blocked-by: P-001 importance: urgent — note: Implemented canonical demo-principal enforcement on CartController and cart.byId, principal-partitioned access classification, and buyer-principal headers on every web REST fallback; verified by full API/web suites and both typechecks.\n- **P-003** `done` Add cross-buyer denial and same-buyer success regressions across controller, named sync query, and web REST helpers; run focused and full API/web verification. blocked-by: P-001, P-002 importance: urgent — note: Added same-buyer, cross-buyer, missing-principal, named-sync, web-header, and no-side-effects-before-owner-check regressions. Current tree verification: API 634 passed/5 pre-existing environment-gated Postgres integration skips; web 571 passed; API/web typechecks green.\n\n\n\n## Decisions\n\n(Use plans:add-decision to append. Each decision is a third-level\nheading with a date line and a body paragraph.)\n",
