          "id": "WI-38710",
          "kind": "bug",
          "title": "Duplicate React in sidestage tree: root react@19.2.8 vs libs/papergrid/node_modules/react@18.3.1 — align papergrid deps so a full root-level vitest run is green (D-017)",
          "state": "done",
          "completedAt": "2026-08-14T07:33:37.613Z",
          "completionAuthority": "committed",
          "completionSummary": "Duplicate React eliminated in the sidestage hive tree. Root package.json now carries overrides {react:^19, react-dom:^19} plus five devDependency pins (@linaria/react ^4.5.4, canvas-hypertxt ^1.0.3, react-number-format ^5.0.0, react-responsive-carousel ^3.2.7, marked ^4.0.10), with a full node_modules+lockfile regen.\n\nTHE AUTHORIZED FIX WAS INCOMPLETE AS WRITTEN — recorded, not quietly widened. The ruling prescribed ONE pin (@linaria/react). Landing exactly that produced 11 failed files / 270 passed tests / ZERO assertion failures: collection-time 'Cannot find package react-responsive-carousel'. ROOT CAUSE: glide-data-grid@6.0.3 declares peerDependencies.react '^16.12.0 || 17.x || 18.x', which EXCLUDES 19; forcing react ^19 via overrides invalidates that peer contract and npm stops materialising glide's dependency subtree. FOUR packages were pruned, not one. @linaria/react was merely the first the suite imported, which is why a single-symptom fix looked complete. Every added pin uses glide's OWN declared range.\n\nWHY NOT THE DEEPER FIX: @glideapps/glide-data-grid@latest IS 6.0.3 (beyond it, only 6.0.4-alphaN). No stable release supports react 19, so declaring glide's deps at root is the only stable path available today.\n\nWHY THE VERIFY TREE'S GREEN DID NOT REPRODUCE: drift, as flagged before landing. verify2 ran 39 files/281 tests; the real tree has 47/326. The newer files import the further-pruned packages. Copying verify2's lockfile across would have masked it.\n\nSCOPE NOTE: libs/papergrid itself was NOT edited (its last commit predates this item). The fix is entirely in the ROOT package.json; libs/papergrid is named only because that is where the duplicate react@18.3.1 materialised.\n\nSAFETY: fleet-warned @fleet:sidestage-dock before the regen (mssm4bz9); held path locks on package.json + package-lock.json under coordination_domain throughout, now released.",
