          "id": "D-013",
          "title": "D-008 mockup gate RATIFIED — P-004 released from needs-human; the D-006 macOS wall is UNCHANGED and still governs how iOS items complete",
          "body": "Date: 2026-08-14\nOWNER APPROVAL: Avi approved the circulated mobile Buyer+Orders design in an owner-verified turn at 2026-08-14T13:37Z, verbatim \"I approve teh mobile design, make sure the fleet implements that now\". Gate sidestage-mockup-approved FIRED 13:37:30.452Z. D-008's stated precondition is satisfied.\n\nACTION: P-004 flipped needs-human -> todo (plan revision seq 48), and its work-item WI-38624 released needs-human -> open. WI-38623 required no action: it is already done (closed 2026-08-14T06:18:39Z).\n\nWHY THIS ITEM AND NOT A BLANKET RE-OPEN. P-004's own text named its blocker verbatim: \"note: D-008 owner-approved mockup gate remains closed; released WI-38624 claim with claimHold so the fleet lane can drain non-UI work.\" WI-38624's checkpoint stated the release condition just as explicitly: \"Resume only after the plan ledger records owner approval opening D-008.\" Both conditions are now met. Its structural dependency is also satisfied: blockedBy:[\"P-003\"] and P-003 is done, unresolvedBlockers:[].\n\nTHE ALTERNATIVE I CHECKED BEFORE FLIPPING — and every future ratifier on this plan should check it too. D-006 establishes a macOS hardware wall: this fleet runs on a Linux host where xcodebuild/xcframework assembly and Swift host-smoke CANNOT run. That wall could independently hold iOS work, and if it were what held P-004 then the owner's DESIGN approval would not have cleared it. It is not: D-006(1) parks macOS-requiring items in state:blocked (e.g. WI-38622 xcframework build), whereas P-004 was needs-human — a distinct state — and its stated cause is the mockup gate alone. An approval of the DESIGN does not and cannot clear a HARDWARE gate; conflating the two would push an item into the pool that physically cannot complete on this host.\n\nSCOPE EXPLICITLY UNCHANGED BY THIS RATIFICATION:\n- D-006(2) still governs HOW P-004 completes here: Linux-feasible source work is claimable; any xcodebuild/simulator verification tail stays parked.\n- D-006(3) stands: the macOS runner gap remains an OWNER-GATED WALL. Either a Mac runner is attached, or iOS items terminate at source-complete + Linux-verified with the build/smoke tail parked.\n- D-001 stands: consume the shared sidestage-core/bindings; never fork core logic.\n\nSTAFFING WARNING for whoever picks this up: this plan currently has NO live members. Its three sidestage-iphone sessions (su-a985d68a, su-cd2b78b7, su-decca8c7) were all verified `ended` at 13:35Z, two minutes before the gate fired. The \"7 waiters woken\" figure reported at emit time counts awaits belonging to ended sessions as live (defect filed as EI-20435738629733639), so the wake reached roughly one agent, not seven. Releasing P-004 makes the work claimable; it does NOT staff it. This lane needs members launched before anything moves.\nRelated: P-004, P-005",
