          "id": "D-014",
          "title": "P-006 released as STALE-blocked (D-008 gate fired); iPhone lane re-staffed; P-002 stays blocked but its recorded blocker is WRONG",
          "body": "Date: 2026-08-14\n[self-imposed leader ruling — su-e1a3a985, 2026-08-14T13:5xZ. Applies the ALREADY-FIRED D-008 gate; does NOT re-open or re-litigate it.]\n\n**1. P-006 was stale-blocked — RELEASED (blocked → todo, WI-38626 synced open).**\nP-006's own item text parked it explicitly: \"D-008 owner-approved mockup gate — visual Buyer browse/search remains parked until a later recorded owner-approval decision opens the gate.\" That gate FIRED 2026-08-14T13:37:30.452Z (Avi, owner-verified turn: \"I approve teh mobile design, make sure the fleet implements that now\"). Its `blockedBy:[P-003]` is done. This is the SAME condition, on the SAME plan, with the SAME text pattern as P-004 — which was released at 13:45Z. P-006 was missed in that pass and sat blocked on a satisfied condition for ~15 min. Corroborated independently: su-3b39b6c3 attempted to file \"clear stale lane-sync blockers (iphone P-002/P-006)\" at ~13:55Z, reaching the same reading from a different direction.\n\n**2. The lane is STAFFED again (it was not — releasing work is not staffing it).**\nAll three prior members (su-a985d68a, su-cd2b78b7, su-decca8c7) were verified `ended`, claims 0, at 13:35Z and again at 13:50Z. Launched sidestage-iphone members on the plan; su-ac465f66 claimed WI-38624 (P-004) at 13:54:27Z. WI-38626 (P-006) was claimed by su-c18bab18 at 13:54:18Z. Both actionable items now have live owners, so NO further members are warranted: P-005/P-007 sit behind them and P-002/P-008 are macOS-walled.\n\n**3. P-002 stays BLOCKED — but its recorded blocker does not say why, and that is a latent trap.**\nMeasured (payload.externalBlockers, 11 rows across the plan): WI-38622's only blocker is `plan-lane:...#P-002` with `capability: live-dependency` — plus a DUPLICATE row of the same ref in status `cleared`. The macOS wall is NOT recorded on it. Contrast WI-38627/WI-38628, which correctly carry `macos-runner:xcode-ios-tests` / `macos-runner:simulator-ipa` at `capability: physical-device`. D-006 explicitly names WI-38622 as macOS-gated (\"xcodebuild/xcframework assembly and Swift host-smoke CANNOT run here\"), so the item is correctly blocked — but for a reason no reader can see from its blocker rows. CONSEQUENCE: the next agent to flip P-002 → todo (exactly what I just legitimately did for P-006) will have the lane-sync clear that live-dependency blocker and hand a Linux host an xcodebuild item. Do NOT flip P-002 on the strength of the mockup approval: a DESIGN approval never clears a HARDWARE gate. The durable fix is a `physical-device` blocker on WI-38622 mirroring WI-38627/38628.\nRelated: P-002, P-004, P-006",
