          "title": "Lane EIs become fleet-admissible via plan_item link, not spec widening",
          "body": "Date: 2026-08-16\nThe fleet claim spec's filter grammar has no OR, so referenced EI bugs (P-001→EI-20538641531453022, P-002→EI-20553580781817620, P-003→EI-20548127444751427, P-004→EI-20547757006412993) are made claimable by writing payload.plan_item on the EI (work_items:update { plan_item: { slug, item } }) — verified 2026-08-16T04:59Z: EI-20548127444751427 claim was refused pre-link and succeeded post-link under the same spec rev 7. Leader pins stay: plan-scoped filter + maxConcurrentClaims=2 (invariant claim-spec-pins-hold polices drift; fleet:launch-on-plan top-ups clobber the cap). CLOSURE NOTE per workspace fact: items carrying payload.plan_item must be closed via work_items:set_state, NOT work_items:complete (sub-lane completion silently closes the parent plan item).",
