          "id": "D-003",
          "title": "P-023 scope correction: EI-20587893882016538 is cannot-reproduce (no code defect); console-clean acceptance = 404-fix deployed + POST-deploy re-verify",
          "body": "Date: 2026-08-16\nP-023's text says both console bugs were \"root-caused with repro\" — that is only true for EI-20589266065184157 (heartbeat 404 loop; fixed in tree at 7eb424f, prod c8eaf164 predates it, 12/12 tests). EI-20587893882016538 (hold-release 400) completed investigation with a RETRACTION of the principal-header-race theory [peer: su-bb5ea5f0, full writeup + retraction on the EI thread, 11:27Z checkpoint on WI-39424]: the cart subsystem's only 400 site is unreachable from client code, removeItem is idempotent (new regression test in apps/api/src/cart/cart.controller.test.ts proves double-release + never-held release are clean), presence-leave 400 ruled out by type narrowing. Verdict: cannot-reproduce unless a fresh occurrence captures the failing request — NOT a release blocker. CONSEQUENCE for the release grade: console-clean acceptance is satisfied by (a) the 404 fix + regression tests landing on prod via the next sidestage deploy, and (b) a POST-deploy live console re-verify through buyer+seller loops — sequenced AFTER WI-39423's paid-order e2e completes (never redeploy prod mid-e2e). The post-deploy re-verify folds into the full-green re-grade evidence pass (leader). [self-imposed sequencing; peer findings per su-bb5ea5f0]",
