          "body": "Date: 2026-08-16\nDate: 2026-08-16. The \"D-024/D-005 governance re-check\" in the P-024 dispatch was under-specified (decision ids without their plan). Resolved by archaeology (WI-39338 checkpoint + plan reads): sidestage prod deploy authority is governed on plan sidestage-auction-chat-public-release-2026-08-14 as a one-shot-per-decision chain — D-023 (wall: later authority required) → D-024 (ec755db, SPENT) → D-025 (48481e4, SPENT) → D-026 (c8eaf164, SPENT = current prod). There is NO live authority for the next deploy. Protocol for P-024 (follows D-026's template exactly): (1) member confirms git-sync committed 7eb424f + the cart regression test to LOCAL sidestage staging and pins the EXACT candidate sha; (2) member obtains a fresh AUTHORITATIVE SIDESTAGE-NATIVE clean-green verdict bound exactly to that pin (pipeline_events cleanGreen=true + runId — NEVER papercusp release:checkpoint-run, per D-025/D-026); (3) member reports pin + verdict ids to leader su-66132; (4) leader records D-027 on the auction plan authorizing exactly one serialized deploy of that pin after dry-run/free-lock/exact-main preflight; (5) member deploys, then post-deploy healthz sha + zero-console re-verify per this plan's D-003. Also ruled: the papercusp green-checkpoint stall (alert 14:2xZ) and the GitHub-bridge push freeze (EI-20582690519832061) are BOTH irrelevant to this deploy — sidestage verdicts come from its native cleanGreen writer, and deploys cut from LOCAL staging. Red or ambiguity is fixed and rerun, never forced.",
