          "completionSummary": "SideStage production build no longer depends on an uncommitted local patch. libs/token-kit was a pinned/detached submodule whose package.json carried a peerDependenciesMeta patch existing in NO git history — the working tree was its only copy, so only this machine could build. Committed that hunk at the pinned commit (b9852732ea6a), pushed + ls-remote-verified to token-kit's origin BEFORE moving the pin, and git-sync swept the superproject pin bump (41160b6). Proven load-bearing by an isolated both-ways probe: a fresh clone now carries the fix and npm ci succeeds, while the same clone with peerDependenciesMeta removed fails with EUSAGE naming style-dictionary missing from the lock file.",
