          "id": "WI-38659",
          "kind": "feature",
          "title": "Hex sweep: migrate stray hardcoded colors in auction.css, BuyerProductRail.css and TSX inline styles onto the token set; add missing role tokens rather than inlining.",
          "state": "done",
          "completedAt": "2026-08-14T05:06:37.655Z",
          "completionAuthority": "committed",
          "completionSummary": "P-003 hex sweep complete. MOST of this item was ALREADY DONE by a prior holder (su-ff5ff3b0) and landed in the 04:54Z git-sync sweep without ever being marked: auction.css and BuyerProductRail.css — the two files named in the item title — were already at ZERO color literals, and every stray the leader's thread comment named (.product-card / .stage-panel / .settings-panel / .readiness-panel navy gradients, .transcript-pane violet, .copilot-panel, and the 'still dark' top nav band) was already migrated onto tokens. I VERIFIED that against the tree and git log rather than rebuilding it. The remaining real work was ONE stray the prior sweep could not have caught: .channel-guide-scrim in events/channel-guide.css hardcoded rgb(0 0 0 / 38%), and that file landed in commit 92c75a9 at 04:59:55Z, AFTER the sweep ran. Fixed per D-002 by adding a named role token (--scrim) rather than inlining — which is what the item title explicitly asks for. Pure black was independently wrong for this theme: styles.css's own token comment states 'Pure black shadows read as grey smudges over cream', so --scrim is expressed in the established warm shadow family as rgb(var(--shadow-hue) / 38%).",
