          "id": "D-006",
          "title": "Extracted seller panels are prop-driven; P-009 supplies props via context/closure, never via dockview panel params",
          "body": "Date: 2026-08-14\nP-008 extracted the two inline SellerTab sections as PURE PRESENTATIONAL components that take every piece of state as an explicit prop:\n\n- `apps/web/src/seller/StageStatusPanel.tsx` — `StageStatusPanelProps` (eventTitle, eventId, onEventIdChange, roomEventId, streamState, streamError, videoRef, isSessionActive, onStartEvent, onEndEvent, onShareRoom, shareDisabled, copyState)\n- `apps/web/src/seller/OnDeckPanel.tsx` — `OnDeckPanelProps` (selectedProduct)\n\nAll stream/room state stays owned by `SellerTab` (useStreamSession / useCopyState / eventId / room). The panels hold no state of their own, so they mount anywhere their props can be supplied.\n\nRULING for P-009 (and it constrains P-010): supply these props through a React context or a closure captured by the panel-component registry — do NOT pass them as dockview panel `params`. dockview serializes `params` into the layout JSON that `toJSON()` produces, which is exactly what P-010 persists to localStorage. Functions, refs (`videoRef`), and live objects are not serializable, so routing them through `params` either corrupts the persisted layout or forces P-010 to strip them back out. Keep `params` to a stable string panel id and resolve everything else from context at render time.\n\nCorollary for P-010: the persisted layout must contain panel IDs and geometry ONLY. A restore path that expects props inside the layout JSON is a bug, not a missing feature.\n\nAlso note (raised by a2076, same fleet): `@papercusp/dock-workbench` already ships a DockWorkspace host + panel registry + localStorage layout store + reset. This decision's constraint holds either way — whichever host P-007 lands on, the panels are prop-driven and the props come from context, not from serialized layout state.\n\nEvidence that the extraction is behaviour-preserving: a temporary parity test rendered the pre-refactor `SellerTab` (git 8126079^) and the post-refactor `SellerTab` with identical props and asserted `renderToStaticMarkup` equality — byte-identical in both the staged-product and empty-on-deck cases (2/2 pass). Permanent markup/aria pin: `apps/web/src/seller/seller-panels.test.tsx` (6/6).",
