          "id": "D-016",
          "title": "Duplicate-React (WI-38699) is LOCAL-TREE-ONLY, not a gate leg — anchor test verdicts on clean-clone evidence, not hive-tree runs",
          "body": "Date: 2026-08-14\nRuling (unchanged): the duplicate-React failure (WI-38699, papergrid react 18.3.1 vs root 19.2.8) does NOT hold the sidestage green-checkpoint red, and gate verdicts are anchored on clean-clone/workspace-scoped evidence. MECHANISM CORRECTED per 598a0 (mssh5xdv, 05:0xZ) — my original body called it a 'local-tree install-state artifact'; that was WRONG: the duplicate React is LOCKFILE-COMMITTED, so it reproduces in ANY clone when tests are invoked at ROOT level (npx vitest run apps/web from repo root → 8 files/19 tests red). The gate stays green because its command is WORKSPACE-SCOPED (npm run test --workspace → 31 files/213 tests green) — a single React resolves under workspace scoping. So the divergence axis is INVOCATION SCOPE, not tree state. Consequences unchanged: (1) WI-38699 fix = dedupe (peer-dep/version alignment in papergrid) so BOTH invocation scopes resolve one React; dev-experience severity, not ship-blocking. (2) Never diagnose gate reds from root-level local runs; the gate-relevant instruments are the workspace-scoped command and the clean clone. (3) Conflicting local measurements between agents were invocation-scope differences, not per-tree divergence.",
