          "completionSummary": "P-015 whole-board resize: IMPLEMENTED, LIVE-VERIFIED (21/21 + screenshots), and one REAL defect found + fixed during that verification.\n\nSHIPPED (sidestage hive tree /home/marsh-office/.papercusp/hives/sidestage, apps/web/src/): seller-dock-store.ts EXTENDED — boardSize is a SIBLING field on P-010's EXISTING row at the SAME key (sidestage.dock:seller), no parallel store; SellerDockBoard.tsx NEW resize frame (pointer + keyboard, E/S/corner); SellerDock.tsx wrap; seller-dock.css chrome (R3 tokens, no hex). Two deliberate store constraints, both tested: the write does NOT bump updatedTs (it is the optimistic-concurrency token useDockLayout replays; bumping it makes the dock's next layout save raise DockLayoutConflictError, which DockWorkspace.persist swallows), and it REFUSES to create a row (a row without layoutJson fails validation and the self-healing store discards it, destroying the user's layout). Default = ABSENCE of boardSize, so CSS and JS cannot drift on the default box.\n\nTHE DEFECT THE LIVE PASS CAUGHT — why this item was NOT done at unit-green: the handles shipped at z-index 2/3 while dockview's splitters (.dv-split-view-container .dv-sash-container .dv-sash) sit at 99. dockview runs those sashes out to the board's outer edges, so the east handle's 6px strip was overlapped along its whole height: document.elementFromPoint() at the east handle's OWN CENTRE returned .dv-sash, and a pointer drag on the width affordance did NOTHING — measured, not inferred: the handle's own listeners recorded ZERO pointer events during a drag. Invisible to every cheaper instrument, which is the point — the component renders, tsc passes, the store round-trips, and KEYBOARD resize works (arrow keys need no hit-test), so the unit suite exercised the identical code path and stayed green while the mouse path was dead. FIX: .seller-dock-board-handle z-index 2->100, --se 3->101. Cost is the last ~6px of each horizontal sash's grab area at the board's outer edge; those sashes stay grabbable across their other ~440px.\n\nRECURRENCE GUARD: 4 new tests in seller-dock-chrome.test.ts assert every handle out-layers dockview's sashes, with the sash z-index MEASURED from the real dockview stylesheet (resolved through the same specifier the app loads) rather than hardcoded — a dockview upgrade that raises it now FAILS the guard instead of silently re-burying the handles. Ships with a CONTROL pinning the shipped 2/3 values as caught against dockview's real 99, plus parser controls.\n\nDISCIPLINE: own playwright-core browser (not the shared verdict daemon, EI-20403007799747278), ISOLATED context so no inherited dock layout could fake a persistence pass (memory 052f015c / EI-18694485377422886), page identity asserted inside the probe, exact values throughout. THREE of my own probe-1 reds were HARNESS faults, corrected before reporting rather than reported then retracted: the board runs 140px below the fold at 1600x1000 so raw page.mouse coords hit nothing (fixed with scrollIntoViewIfNeeded + asserting the handle IS the element at its own centre before dragging); layoutJson is an OBJECT and I had asserted typeof==='string'; updatedTs drifts from the dock's own layout saves and must be measured settled-then-one-resize. Only after those were fixed did the remaining red prove real.",
