      "decisions": [
        {
          "id": "D-001",
          "title": "SideStage owns orders; Stripe only processes payments",
          "body": "Date: 2026-08-14\nThe canonical order, item/source snapshots, buyer ownership, totals, reservation references, payment state, and recovery history live in SideStage Postgres. Stripe receives only the fields needed to execute a payment and returns provider references/events. Orders never reads Stripe to reconstruct purchase history.\nRelated: P-001, P-002, P-005",
          "date": "2026-08-14",
          "itemRefs": [
            "P-001",
            "P-002",
            "P-005"
          ],
          "lineNumber": 94
        },
        {
          "id": "D-002",
          "title": "Extend checkout_order instead of introducing a parallel order system",
          "body": "Date: 2026-08-14\nEvolve the existing checkout_order store into the canonical payable-order surface for cart, auction, and accepted-offer sources. Lift the fields required for ownership, uniqueness, state transitions, and Stripe webhook lookup; keep immutable domain snapshots in the payload. Auction and offer aggregates remain source authorities, but each payable source maps to exactly one canonical order.\nRelated: P-001, P-003",
          "date": "2026-08-14",
          "itemRefs": [
            "P-001",
            "P-003"
          ],
          "lineNumber": 99
        },
        {
          "id": "D-003",
          "title": "Use Restart's Stripe lifecycle, not its unrelated commerce stack",
          "body": "Date: 2026-08-14\nAdopt Restart's server-created PaymentIntent, order-derived idempotency key, Stripe Payment Element, raw-body signature verification, webhook-authoritative state transitions, and redelivery guards. Do not import Restart's Odoo, Signifyd, queue, procurement, standalone checkout-page, or storefront layers.\nRelated: P-002, P-004, P-008",
          "date": "2026-08-14",
          "itemRefs": [
            "P-002",
            "P-004",
            "P-008"
          ],
          "lineNumber": 104
        },
        {
          "id": "D-004",
          "title": "Webhook state is authoritative and side effects are exactly-once",
          "body": "Date: 2026-08-14\nThe browser cannot mark an order paid. A verified Stripe webhook drives processing/success/failure. Duplicate, delayed, or reordered deliveries must not double-commit reservations, double-emit invalidations, or regress a terminal state. Provider events that disagree with SideStage ownership, amount, currency, or metadata are rejected and recorded.\nRelated: P-002, P-003, P-008",
          "date": "2026-08-14",
          "itemRefs": [
            "P-002",
            "P-003",
            "P-008"
          ],
          "lineNumber": 109
        },
        {
          "id": "D-005",
          "title": "Orders is the canonical buyer recovery surface",
          "body": "Date: 2026-08-14\nEvery payable source appears in Orders from SideStage data with explicit source, state, totals, and capability. Payment-required/failed records expose Checkout or Resume checkout into the existing drawer; the auction banner may expose the same action as a convenience. Source-specific prices and IDs are preserved and no auction/offer purchase is rebuilt as an ordinary cart item.\nRelated: P-004, P-005, P-006, P-007",
          "date": "2026-08-14",
          "itemRefs": [
            "P-004",
            "P-005",
            "P-006",
            "P-007"
          ],
          "lineNumber": 114
        },
        {
          "id": "D-006",
          "title": "Principal and reservation contracts are mandatory inputs",
          "body": "Date: 2026-08-14\nThe execution design is required to build on the request-principal/ownership contract tracked in sidestage-demo-user-isolation-2026-08-14 and the reservation/expiry/drawer contract tracked in sidestage-held-items-expiry-checkout-2026-08-14. It may not trust client buyer IDs, create a second identity system, or replace source-tracked cart/auction reservations. P-003, P-005, P-006, and P-008 supply the implementation and verification evidence for this boundary.",
          "date": "2026-08-14",
          "itemRefs": [
            "P-003",
            "P-005",
            "P-006",
            "P-008"
          ],
          "lineNumber": 119
        },
        {
          "id": "D-007",
          "title": "Remove Square rather than preserve a dormant provider toggle",
          "body": "Date: 2026-08-14\nAvi explicitly chose Stripe and does not want SideStage using Square. Remove executable Square server/client paths, credentials, tests, rehearsals, and product copy during cutover. The internal payment seam may remain provider-shaped where it improves testability, but SideStage ships one configured runtime provider: Stripe.\nRelated: P-002, P-004, P-009",
          "date": "2026-08-14",
          "itemRefs": [
            "P-002",
            "P-004",
            "P-009"
          ],
          "lineNumber": 123
        }
      ],
