      "contentHash": "132045cc2ca2799707dc83507a523f091133b85df4b35497b398d043bc869fbd",
      "markdown": "---\ntitle: Implement Drop Runway in the SideStage Watch tab\nslug: sidestage-watch-drop-runway-implementation-2026-08-14\nstatus: shipped\ncreated: 2026-08-15\nupdated: 2026-08-15\n---\n\n## Goal\nReplace the current Coming up / Next in the drop product rail with the selected Drop Runway treatment while preserving real catalog order, hold behavior, availability, and the existing view-all interaction.\n\n## Success criteria\nThe live Watch tab exposes a numbered sale-order runway, accurate current-item progress, responsive horizontal scanning, accessible state and progress semantics, focused regression tests, and verified desktop/mobile rendering.\n\n## Phase — Implementation\n\n- **P-001** `done` Implement the production Drop Runway component, live lineup progress, sequence labels, and responsive styling. importance: high — note: ← WI-39189 completed (done)\n- **P-002** `done` Add focused component and integration regression coverage for numbering, progress, hold states, empty state, and view-all behavior. blocked-by: P-001 importance: high — note: ← WI-39191 completed (done)\n- **P-003** `done` Run focused tests and typecheck, then browser-verify desktop and mobile Watch-tab rendering and interactions with Verdict. blocked-by: P-002 importance: high — note: ← WI-39193 completed (done)\n\n## Decisions\n\n### D-001 — Use Concept 02 Drop Runway\nDate: 2026-08-15\nOwner-selected direction. Preserve the current real catalog data and interactions; adapt the validated Drop Runway comparison concept rather than introducing a parallel product data source. Source decision: sidestage-watch-coming-up-next-mockups-2026-08-14#D-003.\nRelated: P-001, P-002, P-003\n",
