      "slug": "sidestage-watch-live-auction-mockups-2026-08-14",
      "title": "SideStage Watch — improved live auction mockups",
      "status": "ready",
      "updatedAt": "2026-08-15",
      "contentHash": "5be8620302ffa805aa452dacb472e640251467d0e86bfc0dfde6a6d7d2061265",
      "markdown": "---\ntitle: SideStage Watch — improved live auction mockups\nslug: sidestage-watch-live-auction-mockups-2026-08-14\nstatus: ready\ncreated: 2026-08-15\nupdated: 2026-08-15\n---\n\n# SideStage Watch — improved live auction mockups\n\n## Now\n\n**State:** Draft. Plan body to be filled in.\n\n**Next:** human reviews scope and lists Phase 1 items.\n\n## Background\n\n(Why this plan exists; what problem it addresses.)\n\n## Phase 1 — TODO\n\n(Use plans:add-item to populate. Each item is one line:\nsingle id, status token, free text, optional blocked-by.)\n\n\n## Phase — Design and delivery\n\n- **P-001** `done` Audit the current Watch tab, auction interaction states, SideStage tokens, and reusable design-registry components. importance: high — note: ← WI-39146 completed (done)\n- **P-002** `done` Define and validate three improved live-auction UI directions grounded in the existing SideStage design language. blocked-by: P-001 importance: high — note: ← WI-39150 completed (done)\n- **P-003** `done` Generate and assemble the three directions into a responsive comparison gallery. blocked-by: P-002 importance: high — note: ← WI-39151 completed (done)\n- **P-004** `todo` Publish the gallery, verify the public URL resolves, and document the recommended direction. blocked-by: P-003 importance: high\n\n\n\n\n## Decisions\n\n(Use plans:add-decision to append. Each decision is a third-level\nheading with a date line and a body paragraph.)\n\n### D-001 — Target the running SideStage web Watch page, not the native Buyer shell\nDate: 2026-08-15\nCorrection after live verification: the owner-named Watch tab is the running React web surface at the SideStage dev server. Its current auction section uses the cream/red/yellow SideStage web theme and already includes a ring timer, current-price chip, live bid feed, leader/winner banner, and amount form. The earlier SwiftUI/native Buyer audit is adjacent context only and must not govern the mockups. All mockups and specs must use ecosystem react-tailwind and the verified web layout.\nRelated: P-001, P-002, P-003, P-004\n\n### D-002 — Ground concepts in the source tree serving port 5173\nDate: 2026-08-15\nThe authoritative audit source is the live Vite process cwd at /home/marsh-office/.papercusp/hives/sidestage/apps/web (PID provenance re-verified on 2026-08-15), not the stale sibling .sidestage-mobile-source-probe. The live tree's AuctionPanel.tsx and auction.css implement the ring clock, calm/soon/critical urgency, settling and closed phases, recent bid feed, leader/outbid/winner messaging, bid form states, and SOLD stamp on the SideStage cream/red/yellow token system. P-002 through P-004 must preserve those semantics and use the live tree plus /tmp/sidestage-watch-current-tall.png as the visual baseline.\n\n### D-003 — Use one conditional current-offer module in the existing right-hand Watch slot\nDate: 2026-08-15\nDate: 2026-08-15\nOwner correction superseding the three-direction comparison gallery: produce one combined module that preserves the current Now Selling card when no auction is active, then transforms that same right-hand slot in place when an auction is live. The live state includes the ring countdown, current bid, compact bid feed and leader, amount input, and Place bid action. Settling and sold are additional states of the same module. Do not add a separate Live auction block below the video. Replace the prior index.html and concept-specs.json drafts; retain stage-varsity-jacket.png.\nRelated: P-002, P-003, P-004\n\n### D-004 — Chat, Details, and Seller tabs reveal one room-context panel\nDate: 2026-08-15\nOwner approved interactive mockups for all three existing tabs and approved the auction module as-is. The tabs switch one stable panel directly below the video: Chat shows the live thread and composer; Details shows item facts, condition, shipping/returns, and auction terms; Seller shows identity, reputation, verification, follow, and shop actions. The four-state current-offer module remains unchanged in the right-hand slot and stays visible while room tabs switch. Registry-first audit found no tab/chat/profile composite; reuse action.primary, action.secondary, and feedback.banner semantics plus the established SideStage visual tokens.\nRelated: P-003\n",
