          "title": "Parallelize the WS endgame: docs lanes (P-006/007/008) draft NOW in parallel with the P-004 flip; P-004 test sub-lane split to a second member; gate-verify prep staged concurrently",
          "body": "Date: 2026-08-17\n[owner:Avi 2026-08-17 07:49Z interactive, verbatim] \"Can you parralize the websocket work more so that we can get it done quicker?  I checked and we have enough computer, dont worry about that.\"\n\nRULING (fleet leader su-6613215b, executing the owner directive):\n1. P-006, P-007, P-008 blocked-by edges on P-004 are CLEARED for drafting. Docs lanes start immediately, in parallel with the flip. The truthfulness constraint moves from the edge to the completion bar: none of the three may be marked done until the P-004 flip is verified on-tree (leader confirms at gate time). This preserves the intent of the original gating (docs must not claim WS sync before it is real) while removing the serialization.\n2. P-004 itself splits into two parallel strands: su-bb5ea5f0 keeps the main.tsx flip + wiring; su-30669a51 takes the WEBSOCKETS-dispatch test sub-lane (the coverage gap 30669 themselves identified and bb5ea folded into P-004 scope). bb5ea remains the WI-39634 completion owner.\n3. Final-tree gate-verify PREP (clean-clone staging, suite warm-up) starts now (su-03eda174, freshly compacted), so the verify run starts the moment the flip lands rather than after it.\n4. The pool-congestion wake-suppression posture (07:38Z leader-brief) is LIFTED per the owner's explicit compute clearance; parked members may be woken for these lanes.\n\nLane map under this decision: bb5ea→P-004 flip; 30669→P-004 test strand; aa261→P-006 (ArchitectureTab); 7c55c→P-007 (TDD.md); 659a7→P-008 (submission.md+PRD.md); 03eda→gate-verify prep + second witness; 624bb→reserve witness.\nRelated: P-004, P-006, P-007, P-008",
