          "id": "D-007",
          "title": "Gate promotion held by misapplied desktop-perf invariant — land the no-desktop-app SKIP in papercusp NOW; no sidestage exemption; invariant not weakened",
          "body": "Date: 2026-08-17\nFINDING (659a7, msg mswzaem2, evidence-first): the sidestage gate's last 2 runs were suite-GREEN but unpromoted — run trailers: 05:16 7a368bac green=false (real red, since fixed); 06:16 786d291c green=false; 07:16 d8cf3aa0 green=TRUE promoted=false reason=desktop-perf-held; 08:16 fca00c5c green=TRUE promoted=false reason=desktop-perf-held. Mechanism (traced to the writer): green-checkpoint.ts:9462-9465 calls runDesktopPerfGate with only { candidateSha }; desktop-perf-gate.ts falls back to workspace_id='default', whose newest row (06:42:35Z wdio, Papercusp sha c2d7514a) carries invariant webview-http-egress value=-1 (explicit UNMEASURABLE sentinel) ok=false — and the invariant path blocks regardless of block-mode/load. So an unmeasurable PAPERCUSP desktop probe holds promotion for every harness in the workspace, including SideStage, which has no desktop app. This SUPERSEDES the earlier 'gate red = suite failures' framing: the suite causes were real but resolved by 07:16.\n\nRULING [self-imposed leader ratification of 659a7's proposal, 08:36Z]: (1) Land the class fix in the papercusp repo NOW, pre-submission: desktop-perf gate SKIPS when the candidate hive declares no desktop app, mirroring the existing skip patterns in the same run ('no SPA build workspace', 'no lint:tsc script'). (2) NO temporary sidestage exemption — it mitigates one harness and leaves the trap armed for every other non-desktop harness (oddsmith etc. likely also held). (3) Do NOT weaken the invariant itself and do NOT harness-scope the perf-row read (a harness-scoped read returns zero rows for Papercusp too and silently disables a real safety gate). (4) The skip ships with a falsifiability proof per repo guard discipline: a test showing a no-desktop hive skips AND a desktop hive still enforces. (5) The -1-UNMEASURABLE-recorded-as-fail probe behavior is a SEPARATE defect (unmeasurable ≠ breach) — filed as its own item, not fixed in this pass. (6) Acceptance evidence: next sidestage GATE_PROMOTION trailer shows promoted=true (or an explicit non-perf reason). Owner of the fix: 659a7. Consequence for WI-39665 (aa261): a manual checkpoint-run CANNOT unfreeze main until the skip lands — hold fire; close on observed promotion, not suite green.",
