          "id": "D-012",
          "title": "No fleet-spec widening — sidestage-release-drive drains to empty by design; spec_matches_nothing at plan close is the expected terminal signal, not a fault",
          "body": "Date: 2026-08-17\n[self-imposed leader ruling, 2026-08-17 ~09:53Z, in response to 03eda's spec-drain flag msx2029e]\n\nRULING: scheduler claim-spec rev 17 for fleet sidestage-release-drive will NOT be widened. Both id-pinned admission routes (WI-39601, WI-39665) are terminal-done; the only remaining admission route is this cutover plan's own rows, and that is correct: the release drive is in deliberate endgame. Remaining active work is exactly the held closing lanes — P-011 (WI-39663 @624bb), P-012 (WI-39668 + EI-20689489448966446 arming @30669), WI-39672 (@659a7, hardening), WI-39683 (@7c55c) — plus two owner walls (prod deploy go/hold msx1fswr; prod-PG timing mswz208y). Widening the spec would admit unrelated backlog into a release-drive fleet whose mandate is closing, which is scope creep, not utilization.\n\nCONSEQUENCES OTHER LANES MUST FOLLOW:\n1. Idle members without directed work STAND DOWN: park on events:await (fleet-scoped pattern), do not cycle scheduler:get_next against this spec, do not request spec re-authoring.\n2. When the last plan rows close, scheduler:get_next will read `spec_matches_nothing` for this fleet. That is the EXPECTED terminal state under this ruling — the remedy is NOT set_claim_spec widening; it is fleet wind-down (leader runs the acceptance-rubric gate, then fleet:wind-down).\n3. New sidestage work discovered after this point gets filed as normal work-items for the ordinary claimable pool — NOT injected into this fleet's spec.\n\nSequence to wind-down: (a) 624bb's full 100-file leg exit 0 → 30669 arms npm test into greenCmd (closes D-006 item 5); (b) P-011 live-exercise per D-006 serving bar; (c) owner walls resolve or stand as disclosed residue; (d) acceptance rubric authored post-implementation, graded by a NON-implementer; (e) fleet:wind-down.",
