          "id": "D-021",
          "title": "Owner GO on both prod walls: deploy to reviewer-facing prod + prod-PG restart for zero-cache (walls msx1fswr and mswz208y CLEARED)",
          "body": "Date: 2026-08-17\n[owner:Avi 2026-08-17 ~14:05Z — OWNER (interactive) stamped turn] Verbatim: \"go ahead with 1 and 2\", replying to the leader's status enumeration where (1) = deploy to reviewer-facing prod (the msx1fswr wall: prod healthy on e0997f6, candidate carries the WS-cutover delta) and (2) = prod Postgres restart timing for wal_level=logical / zero-cache bring-up (the mswz208y wall, staged procedure + rollback + D-018 publication-parity pre-check).\n\nBOTH OWNER WALLS ARE CLEARED. No prod action was taken before this authorization.\n\nExecution constraints [self-imposed, leader]: (a) The deploy ships a CLEAN checkout of the first TEST-BACKED green main — i.e. after the ~14:16Z gate fire advances origin/main past aa086d8 — not the pre-arming build-only-greened aa086d8, and never the working tree (deploy.sh ships the working tree; use a scratch clean checkout per the msx1fswr next-action). If the fire goes red, hold the deploy leg and escalate the diagnosis back to the owner rather than shipping a cut that predates the serving-lane work. (b) The prod-PG leg executes su-624bb50d's staged procedure with the D-018 publication parity check (pg_publication_tables vs the 20 declared in db/zero-publication.sql) as step 1; the code-independent parts (parity check, wal_level=logical, PG restart, replication verify) may proceed immediately; zero-cache bring-up waits for the deployed code carrying the zero-cache-start.sh preflight guard. (c) Executor: su-624bb50d (staged the procedure, found D-017/D-018); leader executes only if 624bb is unreachable. (d) Completion reports thread msx1fswr (deploy) and mswz208y (PG), and fold into the final owner report.",
