          "id": "D-022",
          "title": "Prod execution order inverted: deploy precedes ALL publication/PG work — targeted_offer reaches prod only via the deploy's migrations",
          "body": "Date: 2026-08-17\n[peer:su-624bb50d finding, ratified by leader 14:2xZ] D-021's constraint (b) assumed the PG leg (publication parity → wal_level → restart) was code-independent and could start before the deploy. 624bb established that is FALSE on prod: public.targeted_offer does not exist there — it arrives only via the deploy's migrations — so CREATE PUBLICATION / the parity ALTERs would abort against the pre-deploy schema. CORRECTED ORDER (supersedes D-021(b) on ordering only, all other D-021 constraints stand): (1) deploy the green main 4bfc31f from a clean scratch checkout; (2) run migrations/verify prod schema; (3) D-018 publication parity check + exact ALTERs — which also answers 624bb's open question of whether anything beyond targeted_offer drifted; (4) wal_level=logical + brief PG restart + replication verify; (5) zero-cache bring-up under the guarded preflight. Executor remains 624bb; rollback staged; reports thread msx1fswr (deploy) + mswz208y (PG).",
