            "testResult": "tsc: exit 0, 0 errors project-wide. WITH SIDESTAGE_PG_INTEGRATION=1: 5 files, 48/48 passed, 0 skipped — --reporter=verbose confirms all 5 contract assertions ran against BOTH stores BY NAME, the PgChatStore legs at 49/11/4/15/17ms (real round-trips to Postgres on 127.0.0.1:55434, not skips). WITHOUT the env var (gate/clean-clone simulation): 41 passed | 7 skipped (48) — the 7 skips are exactly the 5 contract Pg legs + 2 pre-existing pg-chat-store integration cases, so every in-memory assertion still runs in the gate. TEETH VERIFIED, not assumed: extracted the pre-fix chat.store.ts from 5037357^ into a gitignored scratch dir (node_modules/.scratch-*, since removed — the shared tree was never mutated) and ran the contract's replay scenario against it: created=true (contract expects false), replay id 'chat-1-retry' (expects 'chat-1'), countMessages=1 (expects 0), listMessages=['chat-1-retry'] (expects []). The guard fails on the original bug on all four sub-assertions.",
